### Feature Session — login, refresh, logout (OPEN) · perfil y permisos (JWT)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### 1) Login como administrador (OPEN)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Tokens capturados de la respuesta anterior (REST Client)
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}
@refresh = {{login.response.body.refresh_token}}

### 2) Mi perfil y roles (JWT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/perfil
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3) Mis permisos efectivos (JWT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/permisos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4) Renovar tokens (OPEN) — rota el refresh token
# @name refreshed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refresh}}"
}

### 5) Reusar el refresh token ya rotado → 401 y se revoca la familia
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refresh}}"
}

### 6) Cerrar sesión (OPEN)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshed.response.body.refresh_token}}"
}

### Login como operario de planta
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "operador@textilclean.local",
  "password": "Operador123!"
}

### Credenciales inválidas → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "admin",
  "password": "incorrecta"
}
